.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/react-resizable-panels Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "react-resizable-panels"
.PP
React components for resizable panel groups/layouts

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { Panel, PanelGroup, PanelResizeHandle } from "react\-resizable\-panels";

<PanelGroup autoSaveId="example" direction="horizontal">
  <Panel defaultSize={25}>
    <SourcesExplorer />
  </Panel>
  <PanelResizeHandle />
  <Panel>
    <SourceViewer />
  </Panel>
  <PanelResizeHandle />
  <Panel defaultSize={25}>
    <Console />
  </Panel>
</PanelGroup>;
.fi
.PP
.SH "If you like this project, 🎉 \fRbecome a sponsor\fP or ☕ \fRbuy me a coffee\fP"
.PP
.SH "Props"
.PP
.SS "\fRPanelGroup\fP"
prop  type  description  \fRautoSaveId\fP  \fR?string\fP  Unique id used to auto-save group arrangement via \fRlocalStorage\fP  \fRchildren\fP  \fRReactNode\fP  Arbitrary React element(s)  \fRclassName\fP  \fR?string\fP  Class name to attach to root element  \fRdirection\fP  \fR"horizontal" \\| "vertical"\fP  Group orientation  \fRid\fP  \fR?string\fP  Group id; falls back to \fRuseId\fP when not provided  \fRonLayout\fP  \fR?(sizes: number[]) => void\fP  Called when group layout changes  \fRstorage\fP  \fR?PanelGroupStorage\fP  Custom storage API; defaults to \fRlocalStorage\fP \*{1\*}   \fRstyle\fP  \fR?CSSProperties\fP  CSS style to attach to root element  \fRtagName\fP  \fR?string = "div"\fP  HTML element tag name for root element  

.PP
\*{1\*} : Storage API must define the following \fIsynchronous\fP methods:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRgetItem: (name:string) => string\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRsetItem: (name: string, value: string) => void\fP
.PP

.PP
\fRPanelGroup\fP components also expose an imperative API for manual resizing: method  description  \fRgetId(): string\fP  Gets the panel group's ID\&.  \fRgetLayout(): number[]\fP  Gets the panel group's current \fIlayout\fP (\fR[1 - 100, \&.\&.\&.]\fP)\&.  \fRsetLayout(layout: number[])\fP  Resize panel group to the specified \fIlayout\fP (\fR[1 - 100, \&.\&.\&.]\fP)\&.  
.SS "\fRPanel\fP"
prop  type  description  \fRchildren\fP  \fRReactNode\fP  Arbitrary React element(s)  \fRclassName\fP  \fR?string\fP  Class name to attach to root element  \fRcollapsedSize\fP  \fR?number=0\fP  Panel should collapse to this size  \fRcollapsible\fP  \fR?boolean=false\fP  Panel should collapse when resized beyond its \fRminSize\fP  \fRdefaultSize\fP  \fR?number\fP  Initial size of panel (numeric value between 1-100)  \fRid\fP  \fR?string\fP  Panel id (unique within group); falls back to \fRuseId\fP when not provided  \fRmaxSize\fP  \fR?number = 100\fP  Maximum allowable size of panel (numeric value between 1-100); defaults to \fR100\fP  \fRminSize\fP  \fR?number = 10\fP  Minimum allowable size of panel (numeric value between 1-100); defaults to \fR10\fP  \fRonCollapse\fP  \fR?() => void\fP  Called when panel is collapsed  \fRonExpand\fP  \fR?() => void\fP  Called when panel is expanded  \fRonResize\fP  \fR?(size: number) => void\fP  Called when panel is resized; \fRsize\fP parameter is a numeric value between 1-100\&. \*{1\*}   \fRorder\fP  \fR?number\fP  Order of panel within group; required for groups with conditionally rendered panels  \fRstyle\fP  \fR?CSSProperties\fP  CSS style to attach to root element  \fRtagName\fP  \fR?string = "div"\fP  HTML element tag name for root element  

.PP
\*{1\*} : If any \fRPanel\fP has an \fRonResize\fP callback, the \fRorder\fP prop should be provided for all \fRPanel\fPs\&.

.PP
\fRPanel\fP components also expose an imperative API for manual resizing: method  description  \fRcollapse()\fP  If panel is \fRcollapsible\fP, collapse it fully\&.  \fRexpand()\fP  If panel is currently \fIcollapsed\fP, expand it to its most recent size\&.  \fRgetId(): string\fP  Gets the ID of the panel\&.  \fRgetSize(): number\fP  Gets the current size of the panel as a percentage (\fR1 - 100\fP)\&.  \fRisCollapsed(): boolean\fP  Returns \fRtrue\fP if the panel is currently \fIcollapsed\fP (\fRsize === 0\fP)\&.  \fRisExpanded(): boolean\fP  Returns \fRtrue\fP if the panel is currently \fInot collapsed\fP (\fR!isCollapsed()\fP)\&.  \fRgetSize(): number\fP  Returns the most recently committed size of the panel as a percentage (\fR1 - 100\fP)\&.  \fRresize(size: number)\fP  Resize panel to the specified \fIpercentage\fP (\fR1 - 100\fP)\&.  
.SS "\fRPanelResizeHandle\fP"
prop  type  description  \fRchildren\fP  \fR?ReactNode\fP  Custom drag UI; can be any arbitrary React element(s)  \fRclassName\fP  \fR?string\fP  Class name to attach to root element  \fRhitAreaMargins\fP  \fR?{ coarse: number = 15; fine: number = 5; }\fP  Allow this much margin when determining resizable handle hit detection  \fRdisabled\fP  \fR?boolean\fP  Disable drag handle  \fRid\fP  \fR?string\fP  Resize handle id (unique within group); falls back to \fRuseId\fP when not provided  \fRonDragging\fP  \fR?(isDragging: boolean) => void\fP  Called when group layout changes  \fRstyle\fP  \fR?CSSProperties\fP  CSS style to attach to root element  \fRtagName\fP  \fR?string = "div"\fP  HTML element tag name for root element  

.PP
.PP
.SH "FAQ"
.PP
.SS "Can panel sizes be specified in pixels?"
No\&. Pixel-based constraints \fRadded significant complexity\fP to the initialization and validation logic and so I've decided not to support them\&. You may be able to implement a version of this yourself following \fRa pattern like this\fP but it is not officially supported by this library\&.
.SS "How can I fix layout/sizing problems with conditionally rendered panels?"
The \fRPanel\fP API doesn't \fIrequire\fP \fRid\fP and \fRorder\fP props because they aren't necessary for static layouts\&. When panels are conditionally rendered though, it's best to supply these values\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
<PanelGroup direction="horizontal">
  {renderSideBar && (
    <>
      <Panel id="sidebar" minSize={25} order={1}>
        <Sidebar />
      </Panel>
      <PanelResizeHandle />
    </>
  )}
  <Panel minSize={25} order={2}>
    <Main />
  </Panel>
</PanelGroup>
.fi
.PP
.SS "Can a attach a ref to the DOM elements?"
No\&. I think exposing two refs (one for the component's imperative API and one for a DOM element) would be awkward\&. This library does export several utility methods for accessing the underlying DOM elements though\&. For example:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import {
  getPanelElement,
  getPanelGroupElement,
  getResizeHandleElement,
  Panel,
  PanelGroup,
  PanelResizeHandle,
} from "react\-resizable\-panels";

export function Example() {
  const refs = useRef();

  useEffect(() => {
    const groupElement = getPanelGroupElement("group");
    const leftPanelElement = getPanelElement("left\-panel");
    const rightPanelElement = getPanelElement("right\-panel");
    const resizeHandleElement = getResizeHandleElement("resize\-handle");

    // If you want to, you can store them in a ref to pass around
    refs\&.current = {
      groupElement,
      leftPanelElement,
      rightPanelElement,
      resizeHandleElement,
    };
  }, []);

  return (
    <PanelGroup direction="horizontal" id="group">
      <Panel id="left\-panel">{/* \&.\&.\&. */}</Panel>
      <PanelResizeHandle id="resize\-handle" />
      <Panel id="right\-panel">{/* \&.\&.\&. */}</Panel>
    </PanelGroup>
  );
}
.fi
.PP
.SS "Why don't I see any resize UI?"
This likely means that you haven't applied any CSS to style the resize handles\&. By default, a resize handle is just an empty DOM element\&. To add styling, use the \fRclassName\fP or \fRstyle\fP props:

.PP
.PP
.nf
// Tailwind example
<PanelResizeHandle className="w\-2 bg\-blue\-800" />
.fi
.PP
.SS "Can panel sizes be persistent?"
Yes\&. Panel groups with an \fRautoSaveId\fP prop will automatically save and restore their layouts on mount\&.
.SS "How can I use persistent layouts with SSR?"
By default, this library uses \fRlocalStorage\fP to persist layouts\&. With server rendering, this can cause a flicker when the default layout (rendered on the server) is replaced with the persisted layout (in \fRlocalStorage\fP)\&. The way to avoid this flicker is to also persist the layout with a cookie like so:
.SS "Server component"
.PP
.nf
import ResizablePanels from "@/app/ResizablePanels";
import { cookies } from "next/headers";

export function ServerComponent() {
  const layout = cookies()\&.get("react\-resizable\-panels:layout");

  let defaultLayout;
  if (layout) {
    defaultLayout = JSON\&.parse(layout\&.value);
  }

  return <ClientComponent defaultLayout={defaultLayout} />;
}
.fi
.PP
.SS "Client component"
.PP
.nf
"use client";

import { Panel, PanelGroup, PanelResizeHandle } from "react\-resizable\-panels";

export function ClientComponent({
  defaultLayout = [33, 67],
}: {
  defaultLayout: number[] | undefined;
}) {
  const onLayout = (sizes: number[]) => {
    document\&.cookie = `react\-resizable\-panels:layout=${JSON\&.stringify(sizes)}`;
  };

  return (
    <PanelGroup direction="horizontal" onLayout={onLayout}>
      <Panel defaultSize={defaultLayout[0]}>{/* \&.\&.\&. */}</Panel>
      <PanelResizeHandle className="w\-2 bg\-blue\-800" />
      <Panel defaultSize={defaultLayout[1]}>{/* \&.\&.\&. */}</Panel>
    </PanelGroup>
  );
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Be sure to specify a \fRdefaultSize\fP prop for \fBevery\fP \fRPanel\fP component to avoid layout flicker\&.
.RE
.PP
A demo of this is available \fRhere\fP\&.
.SS "How can I set the \fRCSP \fR"nonce"\fP\fP attribute?"
.PP
.nf
import { setNonce } from "react\-resizable\-panels";

setNonce("your\-nonce\-value\-here");
.fi
.PP
.SS "How can I disable global cursor styles?"
.PP
.nf
import { disableGlobalCursorStyles } from "react\-resizable\-panels";

disableGlobalCursorStyles();
.fi
.PP
 
